{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "9f3c1c2e-6b41-4f2a-9a3d-2c1f5b7e8a01",
    "name": "WSI-DMS Integration API v1",
    "description": "Public integration API for the Webfocus Document Barcode and QR Code System.\n\n## Getting started\n\n1. In the DMS, go to **API Applications** (admin only) and register your app.\n2. Copy the token shown once on registration.\n3. In Postman, open this collection's **Variables** tab and set:\n   - `base_url` — e.g. `http://localhost:8000`\n   - `token` — the `wsi_…` token you copied\n4. Run **Meta → Ping**, then **Meta → Me** to confirm the token works.\n\nAuthentication is set once at the collection level (Bearer `{{token}}`), so every\nrequest inherits it. `X-Api-Key: {{token}}` is accepted as an alternative if your\nHTTP client cannot send an Authorization header.\n\n## Field keys are configurable\n\nThe fields a document accepts are managed by the DMS admin in **Settings → Document Form**.\nCall **Meta → Form fields** to discover the current keys instead of hard-coding them —\n`label` and `document_type_id` are the built-in required ones, but an admin can add more.\n\n## Responses\n\nSuccess: `{ \"success\": true, \"data\": … }`\nError:   `{ \"success\": false, \"message\": \"…\" }`\n\n| Status | Meaning |\n| --- | --- |\n| 401 | Missing or invalid token |\n| 403 | Missing permission, deactivated app, or blocked IP |\n| 422 | Validation failed — see the `errors` object |\n| 429 | Rate limit exceeded — see the `Retry-After` header |\n\nThe **Create document** request saves the new id into the `document_id` collection\nvariable, so the requests below it can be run straight away.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "http://localhost:8000",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Root URL of the DMS, without a trailing slash."
    },
    {
      "key": "token",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "API token issued in Settings → API Applications (starts with wsi_)."
    },
    {
      "key": "document_id",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Set automatically by the Create document request."
    },
    {
      "key": "document_type_id",
      "value": "1",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "A valid id from GET /document-types."
    },
    {
      "key": "code_value",
      "value": "DOC-63372",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "A scanned QR / barcode payload, used by the lookup request."
    }
  ],
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "test",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Applies to every request in the collection.",
          "pm.test('Responds with JSON', function () {",
          "    pm.response.to.be.json;",
          "});",
          "",
          "if (pm.response.code === 401) {",
          "    console.warn('401 — check the {{token}} collection variable.');",
          "}",
          "",
          "if (pm.response.code === 429) {",
          "    console.warn('429 — rate limited. Retry after ' + pm.response.headers.get('Retry-After') + 's.');",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Meta",
      "description": "Discovery and health endpoints. Call these first when wiring up a new integration.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Ping",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/ping",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "ping"]
            },
            "description": "Health check. The only endpoint that does not require a token — use it to confirm `base_url` is right before debugging auth."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Me",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Token is valid', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "    const abilities = pm.response.json().data.abilities;",
                  "    console.log('Granted permissions: ' + abilities.join(', '));",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/me",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "me"]
            },
            "description": "Who this token belongs to: application name, granted permissions, the DMS user that owns documents it creates, its rate limit, and usage so far."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Form fields",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/form-fields",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "form-fields"]
            },
            "description": "The fields this DMS currently expects when creating a document, including any custom ones the admin added.\n\nEach entry gives `key`, `label`, `type`, `required`, `value_type`, and either a static `options` list or the endpoint to fetch choices from. Read this rather than hard-coding field names — an admin can change the form at any time."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Document types",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/document-types",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "document-types"]
            },
            "description": "Valid `document_type_id` values."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Users",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/users",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "users"]
            },
            "description": "Valid ids for the `allowed_users` field, when that field is enabled on the document form."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Roles",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/roles",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "roles"]
            },
            "description": "Valid ids for the `allowed_roles` field, when that field is enabled on the document form."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Documents",
      "description": "Requires the `documents:*` permissions granted to the application in the DMS.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create document (QR)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Created', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(201);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
                  "    const doc = pm.response.json().data;",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('document_id', doc.id);",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('code_value', doc.code.value);",
                  "    console.log('Created #' + doc.id + ' — code ' + doc.code.reference);",
                  "    console.log('Code image: ' + doc.code.image_url);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"label\": \"Purchase Order 2026-118\",\n    \"document_type_id\": {{document_type_id}},\n    \"code_type\": \"QR\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/documents",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "documents"]
            },
            "description": "Creates a document and generates its QR code.\n\n**Required:** `label`, `document_type_id`, `code_type` (`QR` or `Barcode`).\nOther keys depend on the admin's form — call **Meta → Form fields** to see them.\n\nThe response includes `code.reference` (the human-facing id, e.g. `#QR-63372`), `code.value` (what is actually encoded in the image) and `code.image_url` (an SVG). Add `?include_code_svg=1` to get the raw SVG markup inline as `code.image_svg`.\n\nRequires the `documents:create` permission. Saves the new id to `{{document_id}}`."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Create document (Barcode, custom code)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"label\": \"Invoice INV-9001\",\n    \"document_type_id\": {{document_type_id}},\n    \"department\": \"Finance\",\n    \"code_type\": \"Barcode\",\n    \"code_value\": \"INV-9001\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/documents",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "documents"]
            },
            "description": "Same endpoint, but supplying `code_value` so the barcode encodes your own reference number instead of a DMS-generated one. Useful when the external system already has its own numbering.\n\n`code_value` must be unique across the DMS — a duplicate returns 422."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "List documents",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/documents?per_page=25&sort=-created_at",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "documents"],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "per_page",
                  "value": "25",
                  "description": "1–100. Defaults to 25."
                },
                {
                  "key": "sort",
                  "value": "-created_at",
                  "description": "created_at | -created_at | name | -name. A leading - means descending."
                },
                {
                  "key": "q",
                  "value": "invoice",
                  "description": "Matches the label, the code reference or the encoded code value.",
                  "disabled": true
                },
                {
                  "key": "type",
                  "value": "Invoice",
                  "description": "Document type name.",
                  "disabled": true
                },
                {
                  "key": "type_id",
                  "value": "1",
                  "description": "Document type id.",
                  "disabled": true
                },
                {
                  "key": "department",
                  "value": "Finance",
                  "description": "Partial match.",
                  "disabled": true
                },
                {
                  "key": "code_type",
                  "value": "QR",
                  "description": "QR | Barcode",
                  "disabled": true
                },
                {
                  "key": "from",
                  "value": "2026-01-01",
                  "description": "Created on or after this date.",
                  "disabled": true
                },
                {
                  "key": "to",
                  "value": "2026-12-31",
                  "description": "Created on or before this date.",
                  "disabled": true
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Returns only the documents **this application** created, newest first, with a `meta` block for pagination.\n\nAn application granted `documents:read-all` sees every document in the DMS instead, including ones created in the web UI.\n\nRequires `documents:read`. Optional filters are disabled by default — tick them in the Params tab."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Get document",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/documents/{{document_id}}",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "documents", "{{document_id}}"]
            },
            "description": "Fetch one document by id. Returns 404 if it exists but belongs to another application.\n\nAdd `?include_code_svg=1` to embed the QR / barcode SVG markup in the response."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Look up a scanned code",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/documents/lookup/{{code_value}}?record_scan=1",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "documents", "lookup", "{{code_value}}"],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "record_scan",
                  "value": "1",
                  "description": "Also increments the document's scan counter."
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Resolve a code straight from a scanner. Matches either the encoded value (`DOC-63372`, `INV-9001`) or the reference (`#QR-63372`), so you can pass whatever the scanner produced.\n\nThis is the endpoint to call from a scanning app; `record_scan=1` counts the scan in the same round trip."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Update document",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"label\": \"Purchase Order 2026-118 (revised)\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/documents/{{document_id}}",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "documents", "{{document_id}}"]
            },
            "description": "Updates only the keys you send — anything omitted keeps its current value. The tracking code cannot be changed once issued.\n\nRequires `documents:update`, and only works on documents this application created."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Record a scan",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/documents/{{document_id}}/scan",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "documents", "{{document_id}}", "scan"]
            },
            "description": "Increments the scan counter for a document you already have the id of, and returns the new total. Use the lookup endpoint instead when you are starting from a scanned code."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Delete document",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/documents/{{document_id}}",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "documents", "{{document_id}}"]
            },
            "description": "Deletes the document and its generated code image. Requires `documents:delete`, and only works on documents this application created."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Error cases",
      "description": "Handy when building error handling on the client side.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "401 — no token",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/me",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "me"]
            },
            "description": "Expected: 401 with a message explaining both accepted header forms.\n\nNote: repeated bad tokens from the same IP are throttled — 20 failures a minute and you start getting 429 instead."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "422 — validation",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"code_type\": \"Fax\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/documents",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "documents"]
            },
            "description": "Expected: 422 with an `errors` object keyed by field — missing `label`, missing `document_type_id`, and an invalid `code_type`. Messages use the labels the admin set on the form."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
